Creates a monitoring job named:
react-app

metrics_path: /probe
Normally Prometheus scrapes:
/metrics
But Blackbox Exporter exposes:
/probe


http://localhost:9115/probe?target=http://APP_SERVER_IP&module=http_2xx
6. Probe Module

params:
  module: [http_2xx]
Tells Blackbox Exporter to use the:
http_2xx
module.
This module checks:

HTTP connectivity
Response status code
DNS resolution
SSL information
Response time


Success occurs when HTTP status is:
200–299

7. Target Definition


static_configs:
  - targets:
      - http://APP_SERVER_IP
This is the actual application being monitored.


targets:
  - http://192.168.1.50

targets:
  - https://my-react-app.com

Blackbox Exporter will send an HTTP request to this URL.

8. Relabeling Explained

initially

source_labels: [__address__]
  target_label: __param_target

__address__ = http://APP_SERVER_IP

It becomes:

__param_target = http://APP_SERVER_IP

This creates the target query parameter for Blackbox Exporter.

Result:



/probe?target=http://APP_SERVER_IP


Step 2

- source_labels: [__param_target]
  target_label: instance

Sets the Prometheus instance label.
Result:


 v            m,   kmkm="http://APP_SERVER_IP"

This makes dashboards and alerts show the actual monitored application instead of the exporter address.

Step 3


- target_label: __address__
  replacement: localhost:9115

Changes the scrape target from:

http://APP_SERVER_IP

to

localhost:9115

which is where the Blackbox Exporter is running.
So Prometheus actually scrapes:

localhost:9115/probe

and Blackbox Exporter probes:

http://APP_SERVER_IP


Prometheus
    |
    | Scrape
    v
Blackbox Exporter (localhost:9115)
    |
    | HTTP Probe
    v
React Application (APP_SERVER_IP)


Prometheus
  -> http://localhost:9115/probe?target=http://10.0.0.5&module=http_2xx

Blackbox Exporter
  -> http://10.0.0.5

React App
  -> returns HTTP 200

Blackbox Exporter
  -> probe_success=1

Prometheus
  -> stores metrics
`


global:
  scrape_interval: 15s

rule_files:
  - alert_rules.yml

alerting:
  alertmanagers:
    - static_configs:
        - targets:
          - localhost:9093

scrape_configs:
  - job_name: react-app

    metrics_path: /probe

    params:
      module: [http_2xx]

    static_configs:
      - targets:
          - http://APP_SERVER_IP

    relabel_configs:
      - source_labels: [__address__]
        target_label: __param_target

      - source_labels: [__param_target]
        target_label: instance

      - target_label: __address__
        replacement: localhost:9115

Useful Metrics Generated
Blackbox Exporter will produce metrics such as:

probe_success

1 = Application reachable
0 = Application unreachable


probe_duration_seconds

Total probe time


probe_http_status_code

200
404
500

probe_ssl_earliest_cert_expiry

SSL certificate expiration timestamp



Purpose of This Configuration
This setup is ideal when your React application does not expose Prometheus metrics. Instead of scraping application metrics directly, Prometheus checks:
✅ Website availability
✅ HTTP status codes
✅ Response latency
✅ SSL certificate health
✅ Endpoint reachability
using Blackbox Exporter running on localhost:9115.
